WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.375
Use the CS lab with a ZVN3310F.

00:00:04.575 --> 00:00:10.847
This captured teaching example uses a ten kilo-ohm drain resistor, a twelve kilo-ohm source

00:00:10.847 --> 00:00:14.879
resistor, and a one hundred microfarad source bypass capacitor.

00:00:15.079 --> 00:00:18.365
These are practice values, not mandatory lab answers.

00:00:19.265 --> 00:00:22.849
Connect the drain resistor from plus fifteen volts to the drain.

00:00:23.049 --> 00:00:26.803
Connect the source resistor from the source to minus fifteen volts.

00:00:27.003 --> 00:00:31.227
The AC input drives the gate, and the output is measured at the drain.

00:00:31.427 --> 00:00:33.667
Follow the labeled transistor terminals.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:39.495
Connect the source bypass capacitor between the source node and zero-volt ground.

00:00:39.695 --> 00:00:44.751
Connect the generator common and both scope references to the same zero-volt ground.

00:00:44.951 --> 00:00:49.047
Minus fifteen volts is a supply rail; it is not the scope ground.

00:00:49.947 --> 00:00:53.787
Return to Measure and open the DC check before testing gain.

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:59.662
With the input signal disabled, inspect the drain and source voltages and the drain current.

00:00:59.862 --> 00:01:02.379
Correct wiring or bias problems first.

00:01:02.579 --> 00:01:05.054
Restore the sine input for the signal test.

00:01:05.954 --> 00:01:12.303
For this example, choose Sine, set amplitude to one hundred millivolts peak, offset to zero, and

00:01:12.303 --> 00:01:13.890
frequency to one kilohertz.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:16.266
The amplitude box uses peak volts.

00:01:16.466 --> 00:01:20.349
One hundred millivolts peak means two hundred millivolts peak-to-peak.

00:01:21.249 --> 00:01:26.667
Choose the input node, VIN, for CH1 and the drain node, VD, for CH2.

00:01:26.867 --> 00:01:31.262
The lab buttons set these probes automatically for a suitable student circuit.

00:01:31.462 --> 00:01:35.729
In a manually opened bench, use the channel menus to choose them yourself.

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:39.125
Press Run and wait for the waveform to settle.

00:01:39.325 --> 00:01:45.272
This captured example shows about zero point two volts peak-to-peak at the input and four point
one

00:01:45.272 --> 00:01:46.322
at the output.

00:01:46.522 --> 00:01:49.765
The inverted output gives a gain of about minus twenty.

00:01:49.965 --> 00:01:53.890
Compare numbers, because the channels may use different vertical scales.

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:58.459
Repeat at ten kilohertz with the same input amplitude first.

00:01:58.659 --> 00:02:01.049
Press Run again after changing settings.

00:02:01.249 --> 00:02:04.299
Record input, output, gain, and any distortion.

00:02:04.499 --> 00:02:10.522
Save labeled waveform captures with the settings visible, and record any later amplitude
adjustment

00:02:10.522 --> 00:02:12.243
in your CS report.
